# aurora.local / packages/home-automation/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/home-automation/pins.env is gitignored (generated by
# `scripts/pin.sh --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated
# recommendations live here. Copy or merge into
# packages/home-automation/pins.env to adopt.
#
# Every pin below is curated and human-reviewed.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# ghcr.io/home-assistant/home-assistant — Home Assistant ships one stable
# release a month (2026.8.0 went stable 2026-08-05) plus weekly Friday
# bugfix-only patches. Pinned to 2026.8.1 (2026-08-07), the latest patch
# on the current monthly line — 8 days old at the time of this check,
# under the usual fortnight caution bar, but HA's own cadence means
# "wait a fortnight" would mean skipping straight to next month's release
# instead, which is worse. Home Assistant's own docs recommend pinning a
# specific version over `:stable` for exactly the reproducibility reason
# this task cares about. Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm64 —
# confirmed. Note 2026.8 drops the default port from 8123 to 80 for new
# installs and removes Companion-app support for iOS 15/watchOS 8/macOS
# 11 — read the release notes if migrating an existing instance. Checked
# 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_HOMEASSISTANT=ghcr.io/home-assistant/home-assistant:2026.8.1@sha256:6340a3de3917a9b19368e767310a96dd090f6a19aca8aeadf87fd1145cec9682

# eclipse-mosquitto — latest 2.x patch is 2.1.2-alpine, released
# 2026-02-09 (over 6 months old, safely stable). Multi-arch: linux/386,
# linux/amd64, linux/arm/v6, linux/arm64/v8, linux/ppc64le, linux/s390x —
# confirmed. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_MOSQUITTO=eclipse-mosquitto:2.1.2-alpine@sha256:6f8d8a947c506f8a2290ec65cd4bd2bc7cb4d43fb5f6271f861cb013e2ef9797

# koenkk/zigbee2mqtt — latest stable is 2.13.0, pushed 8 days before this
# check. Multi-arch: linux/386, linux/amd64, linux/arm/v6, linux/arm/v7,
# linux/arm64, linux/riscv64 — confirmed, so arm64 (Pi) is fine; only
# very old armv6-class Pi Zero/1 boards need the documented
# `--platform linux/arm/v6` override due to a known Docker
# architecture-selection bug on that specific hardware. Checked
# 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_ZIGBEE2MQTT=koenkk/zigbee2mqtt:2.13.0@sha256:4fb4db4d49a217bed6d0204f454ce809febc565bbe051b85c556ee2bcef73d8c
